skate3-gmod

native/skate-bridge/src/rails.rs and parts of native/skate-bridge/src/collision.rs
are ported from 2010 Rust Rewrite Mashup by chasmlol
(https://github.com/chasmlol/2010-rust-rewrite-mashup, commit f608f85),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Changes: the math types come
from glam instead of Bevy, and MW2-specific extraction was removed.

setup/convert.py is adapted from that project's skate/converter/iw4l_skate_convert.py
under the same license.

The playermodel retarget in addon/lua/skate3/cl_skater.lua is ported from that
project's crates/render_anim/src/skate/rig.rs, and the board import in
native/gmod-skate/src/skater.rs follows its crates/assets/src/skate_board.rs,
under the same license.

native/patches/skate-host-hud.patch modifies that project's skate-host crate
(at the same commit) to report the trick line in progress and set the skater's stance, under the same
license. CI applies it to a fresh clone; none of that crate is copied here.

The setup app bundles vgmstream-cli (https://github.com/vgmstream/vgmstream),
which decodes the sounds on the player's own disc. Its licence ships beside it
as COPYING; the Windows build's FFmpeg and codec libraries are vgmstream's own
distribution, unchanged.

Which Skate 3 sound ids play the pops, landings and grind hits, and the
layout of the game's SPLC sound banks, come from the reverse-engineering notes
in doriangironde/skate-3-rust-macos (https://github.com/doriangironde/skate-3-rust-macos)
and Hailey-Ross's audio work on SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine (PR #32). No
code is taken from either; setup/audio.py is written from those notes.

The rules for the footsteps, the wheels' spin-down and the bail hits in
addon/lua/skate3/cl_sounds.lua follow SK8-ENGINE's crates/skate-audio
(https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine, GPL-3.0), its port of the
game's audio code: the sound ids, curves and thresholds are taken from it.
setup/audio_tuning.py ports the part of its tools/asset_pipeline/audio_export.py
that reads the collision tuning from the player's own disc (GPL-3.0, the same
licence as this project).

The session marker's static in addon/lua/skate3/cl_marker_static.lua is a
port of SK8-ENGINE's crates/skate-game session_marker/effect.rs, effect.wgsl
and noise.rs (GPL-3.0): retail's noise generator, texture and postfx noise
pass, redone with render targets; the marker's sounds are the front-end
events its session_marker/mod.rs posts.

The pop, landing and take-off whoosh rules, the seam clicks, the choice of
Skate 3's material for a surface and the name of the multiplier chimes in the
same file follow how SK8V (https://github.com/becaring/SK8V, Apache-2.0) plays
Skate 3's sounds in GTA V; its notes on retail's field keys and rules are read,
no code is taken. setup/audio_tuning.py reads those fields from the player's own
disc.

native/skate-xma is SK8V's EA-XMA decoder (https://github.com/becaring/SK8V,
rust/skate-xma, LGPL-2.1-or-later, a port of FFmpeg 4.4's XMA path; its licence
text is native/skate-xma/COPYING.LGPL). native/skate-xex is SK8V's XEX reader
(rust/ped-export, Apache-2.0). setup/audio_cache.py and setup/audio_blobs.py
port SK8V's tools/prepare-skate-audio.py and tools/prepare-audio-tuning.py
(Apache-2.0): they unpack and decode the player's own Skate 3 audio into a local
cache for the retail-sound engine. Nothing from the disc is shipped.

native/skate-aems is SK8V's port of Skate 3's AEMS audio runtime
(https://github.com/becaring/SK8V, rust/skate-aems, Apache-2.0), itself
translated from the game's retail executable. native/gmod-skate/src/audio.rs
and audio_map.rs are adapted from its skatev-runtime (Apache-2.0): the first
runs the engine on a thread and plays it on the default output device, the
second turns the session's state into the sound scripts' game variables.
native/patches/skate-host-zzz-audio.patch is its engine patches 0009 and
0022 to 0025 (Apache-2.0) fitted to the engine this mod builds on; they publish
the skater's audio state read-only. The engine plays only from a cache built
on the player's machine out of their own disc.

setup/skate3_formats/ reads the park pieces and the Mega Park stadium off the
player's own disc. archive.py, arena.py, geometry.py, world_materials.py and
world_textures.py come from NativeX World Studio
(https://github.com/NativeXex/nativex-world-studio-skate3), MIT licensed
(LICENSE-NativeX.txt); archive.py is changed to read stored chunks.
skate3_streams.py and retail_collision_mesh.py come from SK8-Engine
(https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/SK8-Engine, tree 311cd40), MIT licensed
(LICENSE-SK8-ENGINE.txt), as NativeX vendors them. See that folder's README.

setup/physbox.py writes the ground's collision solid for addon/maps/*.bsp. The
byte layout of a vphysics box solid (what Source's .phy files and a map's
physcollide lump hold) was learned from a box .phy that ships with Garry's
Mod; the file only supplies the generic 12-triangle box topology, and every
coordinate and size in it is rewritten.

setup/setup_fonts.py embeds Jost (Latin subset, regular and bold) for the
setup page, SIL Open Font License 1.1, Copyright 2020 The Jost Project Authors
(https://github.com/indestructible-type/Jost); the licence text is in that file.
